# Karpenter Live Validation Deployment

## Goal

Deploy the existing Go controller and Helm chart to a new isolated AKS cluster.
Do not modify the existing Terraform-owned cluster or the old fork checkout.

## Resources

- Resource group: `rg-karpenter-validation-20261011`, eastus2.
- Node resource group: `rg-karpenter-nodes-20261011`.
- Kubernetes 1.35.8, one `Standard_D2s_v5` system node in zone 1.
- The system pool has no custom taints so AKS Run Command can schedule. Test Pods
  explicitly select their Karpenter NodePool and cannot fall back to the system pool.
- Private link-based API server; administration through AKS Run Command, no public SSH.
- Azure CNI overlay with Cilium; AKS-managed node VNet, standard load-balancer
  outbound configuration, node public IPv4, no NAT GW. A separate private subnet
  with implicit outbound disabled is used only for the image builder. Live tests
  must prove whether node traffic uses its own IP rather than LB SNAT.
- Basic ACR for the controller image, managed identities and scoped AcrPull.
  Controller provisioning roles are scoped to the node resource group after
  cluster creation. No extra bootstrap artifact cache is requested.
- At most one ordinary `Standard_D4ds_v6` test worker at a time and a disposable
  image builder. The AMD v6 candidate was subscription-restricted in this region.

## Execution

1. Compile Bicep and validate the selected Kubernetes/SKU/quota inputs.
2. Create only the new resource group, run ARM what-if, then deploy the template.
3. Build the repository's controller image and test it locally before pushing.
  Use `infra/validation/ko.yaml` for a static Linux validation binary from macOS;
  the upstream CGO-enabled release configuration is not modified. This run does
  not certify the release build's FIPS/CGO configuration.
4. Configure Workload Identity and deploy the existing Helm chart through Run Command.
5. Pin official AKS Ubuntu 24.04 Gen2 CIG `202610.08.0` for the builder.
6. Test official CIG + NVMe + direct public-IP egress; then create, generalize,
   publish, and test a custom Gallery image with a unique build marker.
7. Test Spot max price, image drift/replacement, failed creation, and cleanup.
8. Remove temporary Pods, NodeClaims and builder resources; retain only the
   explicitly reported cluster/image resources for user inspection.
  Pause the validation NodePool at zero CPU before reducing the system pool,
  so background system/management demand cannot create another worker.

## Evidence

ARM preflight rejected both the BYO-node-VNet/managed-cache combination and
Workload Identity with outbound type none. The compatible fallback retains
Workload Identity and node public IPs with a managed LB. The LB resource can have
fixed charges even when node traffic bypasses its SNAT; do not report zero-LB.

Use the existing provider tests, local container startup, actual node Ready/Pod
success, VM image/billing/disk metadata, observed public egress IP, and resource
cleanup. Record results in `docs/runtime-validation-report.md` and configuration
examples in `docs/upstream-porting.md`. Never print credentials or bootstrap tokens.

## Existing Cluster Helm Upgrade Validation (2026-10-11)

- Upgrade this isolated cluster only to the verified Quay `v20261011-dev` digest;
  use the source-matched local controller and CRD charts.
- Existing objects were rendered/applied manually. Explicitly inspect ownership,
  adopt only matching unmanaged objects, and reject another release's resources.
- Discover Azure metadata and configure/reuse scoped Workload Identity. Keep
  bootstrap token reads and storage in-cluster; generated values use Secret refs.
- Legacy system VMSS has no live instances and D2s_v5 reallocation was rejected.
  Restore administration with a D4ds_v6 system pool in the same test cluster;
  do not change the unrelated Terraform cluster or use GPU resources.
- appType: Kubernetes controller (no browser tier). Docker and Node.js are available;
  use shell/Helm checks, seven offline safety cases, actual Kubernetes/ARM journeys.
- Reuse official/custom/Spot/rejection/cleanup scripts with new public-IP API;
  add default-no-IP, legacy-field, auto-disk and invalid-configuration journeys.
- PASS requires actual command exit zero, controller readiness and pinned digest,
  node/Pod readiness, observed egress vs Azure address, requested image/NVMe/Spot
  metadata, and independent absence of VM/NIC/disk/IP after each deletion.
- Keep at most one four-CPU test worker active. Pause the pool before final cleanup;
  retain only a healthy management system pool and reported image/registry resources.
- Boundaries: live aksscriptless/Ubuntu2404/CPU only. GPU API admission is not GPU
  runtime validation; Machine API and advanced security still have local coverage
  only unless a separate suitable live environment is provisioned.